BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (number of precepts of which logic is composed, I believed that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (four following would prove perfectly sufficient for me, provided I) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (took the firm and unwavering resolution never in a single instance to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (fail in observing them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 282.00 Td (The first was never to accept anything for true which I did not clearly) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 267.00 Td (know to be such; that is to say, carefully to avoid precipitancy and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 252.00 Td (prejudice, and to comprise nothing more in my judgement than what) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 237.00 Td (was presented to my mind so clearly and distinctly as to exclude all) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 222.00 Td (ground of doubt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 203.00 Td (The second, to divide each of the difficulties under examination into) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 188.00 Td (as many parts as possible, and as might be necessary for its adequate) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 173.00 Td (solution.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 154.00 Td (The third, to conduct my thoughts in such order that, by commencing) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 139.00 Td (with objects the simplest and easiest to know, I might ascend by little) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 124.00 Td (and little, and, as it were, step by step, to the knowledge of the more) Tj ET
