BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 516.10 Td (And finally, as it is not enough, before commencing to rebuild the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 501.10 Td (house in which we live, that it be pulled down, and materials and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 486.10 Td (builders provided, or that we engage in the work ourselves, according) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 471.10 Td (to a plan which we have beforehand carefully drawn out, but as it is) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 456.10 Td (likewise necessary that we be furnished with some other house in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 441.10 Td (which we may live commodiously during the operations, so that I) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 426.10 Td (might not remain irresolute in my actions, while my reason compelled) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 411.10 Td (me to suspend my judgement, and that I might not be prevented from) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 396.10 Td (living thenceforward in the greatest possible felicity, I formed a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 381.10 Td (provisory code of morals, composed of three or four maxims, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 366.10 Td (which I am desirous to make you acquainted.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 68.00 347.10 Td (The _first_ was to obey the laws and customs of my country, adhering) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 332.10 Td (firmly to the faith in which, by the grace of God, I had been educated) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 317.10 Td (from my childhood and regulating my conduct in every other matter) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 302.10 Td (according to the most moderate opinions, and the farthest removed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 287.10 Td (from extremes, which should happen to be adopted in practice with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 272.10 Td (general consent of the most judicious of those among whom I might) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 257.10 Td (be living. For as I had from that time begun to hold my own opinions) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 242.10 Td (for nought because I wished to subject them all to examination, I was) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 227.10 Td (convinced that I could not do better than follow in the meantime the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 212.10 Td (opinions of the most judicious; and although there are some perhaps) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 197.10 Td (among the Persians and Chinese as judicious as among ourselves,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 182.10 Td (expediency seemed to dictate that I should regulate my practice) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 167.10 Td (conformably to the opinions of those with whom I should have to live;) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 152.10 Td (and it appeared to me that, in order to ascertain the real opinions of) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 137.10 Td (such, I ought rather to take cognizance of what they practised than of) Tj ET
