BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 541.00 Td (giving a summary of the contents of this treatise. It was my design to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 526.00 Td (comprise in it all that, before I set myself to write it, I thought I knew) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 511.00 Td (of the nature of material objects. But like the painters who, finding) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 496.00 Td (themselves unable to represent equally well on a plain surface all the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 481.00 Td (different faces of a solid body, select one of the chief, on which alone) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 466.00 Td (they make the light fall, and throwing the rest into the shade, allow) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 451.00 Td (them to appear only in so far as they can be seen while looking at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 436.00 Td (principal one; so, fearing lest I should not be able to compense in my) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 421.00 Td (discourse all that was in my mind, I resolved to expound singly,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 406.00 Td (though at considerable length, my opinions regarding light; then to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 391.00 Td (take the opportunity of adding something on the sun and the fixed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 376.00 Td (stars, since light almost wholly proceeds from them; on the heavens) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 361.00 Td (since they transmit it; on the planets, comets, and earth, since they) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 346.00 Td (reflect it; and particularly on all the bodies that are upon the earth,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 331.00 Td (since they are either colored, or transparent, or luminous; and finally) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 316.00 Td (on man, since he is the spectator of these objects. Further, to enable) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 54.00 301.00 Td (me to cast this variety of subjects somewhat into the shade, and to) Tj ET
